  "instructions": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "kind": "prep",
      "primary_message": "Juice the limes. Rinse the quinoa. Peel and shred the carrot. Peel, seed, and finely dice the cucumber. Finely chop the scallions. Chop the fresh cilantro.",
      "secondary_message": "3 limes\n1 cup quinoa\n1 carrot\n1 small cucumber\n2 scallions\n¼ cup fresh cilantro"
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "primary_message": "Add quinoa, salt and 1-2/3 cups water to a medium saucepan. Bring to a boil and then reduce heat to low, cover, and cook for 15 minutes, until the water is absorbed and quinoa is cooked. Transfer to a serving bowl and let cool.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "primary_message": "In the meantime, make the dressing by combining the lime juice, Asian fish sauce, vegetable oil, sugar and crushed red pepper flakes in a medium bowl. Whisk until the sugar is dissolved. Add shrimp to the dressing and let marinate until ready to assemble the salad.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "primary_message": "Once quinoa is cool, add red bell pepper, carrot, cucumber and scallions to the bowl. Right before serving, add the dressing, shrimp and cilantro and toss well. Taste and adjust seasoning with more salt, sugar or crushed red pepper flakes if necessary. Serve cold.",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
